<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
  Copyright (C) 2026 CARLOS Contributors

  Context descriptor for DrugRef2, installed by the carlos-emr-drugref
  package.

  DrugRef speaks unauthenticated XML-RPC: anything that can reach
  /drugref2/DrugrefService can query the drug database and, more to the point,
  reach a servlet whose only access control is the network. It is therefore
  gated twice:

    1. nginx never proxies /drugref2 — the front door has no route to it.
    2. The RemoteCIDRValve below refuses any request whose (RemoteIpValve-
       resolved) client address is not the host loopback.

  The valve is declared HERE, in an external context descriptor, rather than
  relying on the one inside the WAR's META-INF/context.xml: that in-WAR valve
  uses a "${...:127.0.0.1/32,::1/128}" placeholder default, and
  RemoteCIDRValve splits `allow` on commas *before* property substitution, so
  the placeholder never parses. An external descriptor takes precedence over
  the packaged one, which is also why deployXML must stay at its default.

  `allow` is the valve's ONLY address attribute and it takes IPv4 and IPv6
  CIDRs in one comma-separated list. (There is no allowIPv6 attribute; naming
  one makes Tomcat reject the descriptor and the context never deploys.)

  The Host-level RemoteIpValve in server.xml runs BEFORE this one and has
  already replaced the peer address with the real client address from
  X-Forwarded-For. That is what makes this gate meaningful: a request arriving
  through nginx presents the browser's address here and is refused, while
  CARLOS's own in-process call arrives from 127.0.0.1 with no forwarded header
  and is allowed.
-->
<Context docBase="/usr/share/carlos-emr/webapp/drugref2"
         reloadable="false"
         crossContext="false"
         useHttpOnly="true"
         privileged="false">

    <Valve className="org.apache.catalina.valves.RemoteCIDRValve"
           allow="127.0.0.1/32,::1/128"/>

    <Resources cachingAllowed="true" cacheMaxSize="20480" cacheTtl="60000"/>
</Context>
